                <pb facs="0495" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg415"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/495: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hibbard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-29T11:00:00-04:32">May 29, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>31. My telegram No. 30, May 28, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d411-f1"/> President
                    Siles resigned last night turning over the Executive power to the Cabinet.
                    Elections for a constituent assembly to revise the Constitution have been called
                    for June 29. The assembly will be composed of the usual number of Senators and
                    Deputies making up Congress and will meet on July 28th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hibbard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
